First, let me state that I love ketchup, and I tend to get angry when I buy
fries, and open the bag to find no ketchup.

Now fries can exist without ketchup, but that begs the question "What good
are fries without ketchup?"

As a side note, if you want your fries with mustard, mayo, or vinegar - I'd
suggest you order them that way, 'cause there's no way in hell that the guy
at Wendys is going to assume you want them that way....

 Now, back to my point. Is the oil/grease part of the fry? I've tried those
baked potato stick thingies, but they tend to bend too much under the weight
of the dern ketchup. Notice that I refer to them as "baked potato stick
thingies" because they can not be fries, because fries must be *fried* to be
fries. I'll assume here that in order for something to be fried, an oil or
grease of some sort must be used. This would tend to make me think that
grease is a required ingredient of fries. Now does this mean that oil/grease
is part of the fry? I sure think so.. it's there, and it HAS to be there.
Without the oil/grease what would the fry be cooked in? Water? Naw... then
the'd be "poached", and there's no way that I'm going to order a large
"poach" with my Quarter Pounder!

    What about salt? Some places (like the local McD's) have taken up the
anoying habit of sometimes putting salt on the fries straight out of the
fryer, while at other times they TRY to be healthy and leave the stuff off.
This leaves ME in a very tough spot. If I ask for salt on my fries, then I
take the chance that the window waiter will think that I mean to add salt to
the fries at all cost - in other words, add salt to the already salty fries!
BTW, this is very similar to the on again/off again practice of putting
ketchup in the bag automatically. If I ask for it, I rick getting double the
ketchup... but I'm drifting off of my point again.

    I also wonder about the little bag/box they put the fries into. Are they
part of "fries?" The last time I took the wife out for a night on the town,
we started the ball moving at "Rootys". Now I know "Rootys" is not a
national burger chain, but the point I'll make with this one will be
universal anyways. Back to the story - we were waiting at the table when the
nice wait person brought out our meals. When asked, I directed the grilled
chicken sandwich to my Love, and the 1/2 pound burger with extra fat to
myself. Then something happened that now seems to be significant! She asked
which one of us ordered the "atomic chilli cheese fries!"  What I was handed
was not a pile of potato/grease/beef/jalapeno/cheese, it was a pile of
potato/grease/beef/jalapeno/cheese in a BOX!!!! Now did she mean to imply
that the box was part of what was collectively called "attomic chilli cheese
fries", or did she mean "atomic chilli cheese fries IN A BOX?" Either way, I
felt pretty bad when we left - even worse when we got to our final
destination, Putt-Putt land!  God, was my wife happy to finally have an
evening like that. We finally go out for one stinkin' night without us
droping by the local computer store,  which always leads to me bitching
about the lack of Alpha compatible stuff, and the over-abudance of Mac
compatible stuff....

  The bottom line of all of this is this, I'm really starting to like
Wendys. They ALWAYS salt their fries, ALWAYS put them in a box. Best of all,
they have a big damn sign that reads "Ketchup available upon request."

Just some thoughts,
Clint

P.S. I hope no one minds if we rename this thread....

