Good question. I was not acting in my Charlie Matco capacity at that
time and consequently did not author that rumour.

While it is true that Digital in 1992-1993 was projecting EV6 in 1996,
the firm subsequently backed off the predictions. I believe it was three
years ago at Microprocessor Forum that DEC first spoke of the chip. At
the subsequent ISSCC '96 (?) conference they indicated that production
was at least a year off, e.g. 1997.

575MHz chips are in production now, as are other bins. I still believe
that EV6-based servers and upgrades will ship this year. Samsung has an
even more aggressive schedule... CMOS7 shrink of their currently-
available EV6 parts will be out early next year. Samsung had operational
prototype EV67 silicon last November.

Incidentally, on August 27 the EV6 workstation upgrade sales pitch at
http://www.workstation.digital.com was revised to reflect the new
shipment schedule.

