When using C, you have to do it with conventions and code discipline.
On C/VMS, for example, the dsc$ structures are used to describe the
various safe string types for use with the native VMS runtime
libraries.  But using them does rely on discipline.  It doesn't
provide true type safety.  If you want that, you need to move to
C++ or another strongly-typed language.

