MerefBast wrote:
> 
>    Anyone happen to know how many processors DEC-UNIX, OpenVMS, and ULTRIX can
> support in a single computer? Does it vary by underlying processor (VAX, Alpha,
> MIPS)? Got any URLs or other references I could look at?

Well, as Shannon Knows DEC subscribers are aware:

Digital UNIX: 14 CPUs (AlphaServer 8400)
OpenVMS: 14 CPUs (AlphaServer 8400)
Ultrix: 4-6, I believe, in an antiquated DECsystem derivative of the VAX
6000 Calypso platform

Note that CPU limits on DUNIX and OVMS will increase dramatically when
the next-generation switch-based WildFire Global Server debuts.

Initial limit is likely to be 32, thence moving to 64 and beyond. OVMS
will rely on Galaxy APMP; DUNIX will implement a more ccNUMA-like
approach.

