: .uni-siegen.de> wrote:
:>Mike Trettel <possum@tree.branch> wrote:
:>
:>Btw., you can always use a dumb serial terminal as console ...
:>
:>Hope that helps,
:>	Michael

I just looked it up - the DEC part no. for the monitor cable is BC 29G-08.

: Actually, yes it does.  Any suggestions as to how I can hook it to my 
: Linux box through the serial port would be appreciated. 

A simple three-wire cross-over serial cable will do the trick. You'll have
to cross lines 2 and 3 (transmit and receive data) and put line 7 straight
through (GND) - assuming you have a 25 pin SUB-D connector on the Linux side.
For terminal emulation, you can use Minicom. Simply set the serial line
parameters to 9600 baud, 8 bits, 1 stop bit, no parity.

: I suppose I could 
: round up an old IBM or DEC terminal until I find a cable-should cost 
: around $5.00 or so.  Big hamfest coming up soon in Gaithersburg, MD 
: soon...

Be careful when buying old IBM terminals - some of these come with "funny"
synchronous interfaces instead of a RS232 interface. DEC terminals should
be fine - a VT420 is a rather nice one ...

regards,
	Michael
