cxx 6.1 will be out soon (beta testing is at the sanity kit/critical
bug fix state). The compiler/library is very good and another
significant step forward. You can try to contact Digital to get the
sanity kit for testing, otherwise you will find the beta version 
at  ftp gatekeeper.dec.com  in  /private/deccxx as  CXX610T25.tar

Install using setld as usual after deleting the old subsets starting 
in CXX.... 

Of course your problems might be due to code specific things, overly
heavy template code, massive inlining, aggressive optimization on
large subroutines, etc.  We have seen a previous versions of KAI C++
crashing (and the CRAY version of that compiler still crashes on
some code.) after allocating more and more memory. Try the new version!

