Wayne W. Scott <wscott@nac.net> wrote:
}What are these EV* mnemonics all about?
}Is there a chart or table that shows what they mean?

   "EV" is more or less DEC's quaint way of saying "generation".

        EV4  = 21064
        EV5  = 21164
        EV6  = 21264
        EV7  = 21364

   then there are the "process shrink" intermediate versions
   that any sane person would call "EV6.5" or something, but
   which get called "EV67" (6 shrunk to 7 dimensions).
   (taking a microprocessor and shrinking all its dimensions
   makes it faster).

