Alpha NT is just like Intel NT. M$ did so far a good job on this.
But applications is the problem. M$ does provide Word and Excel, but not
Powerpoint (means Office Package is incomplete). They provide Exchange
Server and Client and Outlook Express for Alpha, but not Outlook 97.

You can have some Alpha NT printer drivers for HP printers, but only from
M$, not from HP (remember HP sees MERCED and not Alpha as its future).

Alpha is unbeatable in the CAD market with native applications, but with
all other applications you have a hard time finding the right way.

Another example: There is M$ Internet Explorer for Alpha NT (current and
with add-ons), but NETSCAPE for Alpha NT is still V3 and unsupported.

But: 64bit applications are currently only Alpha. So if you need more than
32bit, Alpha is years ahead of INTEL.

>                                          Are they much more expensive
>than normal Intelly PC:s and are much faster?

It depends. Alpha _is_ generally faster than INTEL, but with the delay
of the new Alpha Chip 21264, INTEL reduced the gap the last months (and
as ever before newer INTEL chips are faster than older Alphas)

Currently price/performance is better on INTEL but may again change with
the 21264. And buying a PC today, means next month you can get the same PC
for less.

