for x86-Processors, both without any Manual or other Info. The Board should
be out from an ALPHA XL 266. It looks like a modern ATX-Board, there�s also
a connector that looks like one for a ATX-Power-Supply. And there are three
(instead of two like on a "standard PC-Board") Connectors for a
AT-Power-Supply. There are descriptions for the Jumpers on the Board, but
not for the connectors.
The CPU-Card I got  has two Socket5�s and an slot for a PB-Cache-Module.
So now my Questions:

* What intel CPU�s can I use in that CPU-Board? (As I know Socket5 goes up
to 133MHz, right?)
* Is it possible to put the board in an ATX-Case and use it with an
ATX-Power-Supply (Connector J18)? If Yes, where do I connect the ON-Switch?
(Perhaps J31?)
* If not, can I use a standard AT-Power-Supply? What for is the 3rd
Power-Connector (J14)?
Has someone the pin-out?
* What type of RAM (FPM, EDO, with or w/o Parity) can I use?
* Where can I get an BIOS-Update? Digitals Website for the XL 266 shows only
items for AXP-CPU�s!
* What for are J100 and J101 on the CPU-Board? J101 has a little PCB on it,
but with no electronic parts!?!
* I heard the board has also an IDE-Port beside his SCSI-Controller. Is this
true???

If someone has any helpfull informations, please send it to
