As you have already seen, onsale is selling alphastations left and
right.  I bought one of these stations and am pleased to see it in
perfect condition.   But  there has been one stubling block for this
whole deal and it is that (and i knew this in the back of my head when i
bought it) this series of AS200 only came with enough flash ram to hold
either the SRM  OR the ARC not both at one time.  The system came with
the SRM (6.2-2) loaded by default and works fine from a firmware POV.  I
would gladly update the firmware to the ARC/newer verion if iI had a
firmware CD and/or a CD-ROM drive, but i dont :(  I know that it is
possible to update the firmware via a floppy disk but i have tried all
the methods described in all of the docs and i keep getting "failed to
open dva0...".  The only OSs that i have to work with to make the disk
are Linux and DOS.  If someone knows some nifty little trick to get this
thing to work, dont keep it a secret.

