The cute things about disktab is that you really donb't need one.

I was planning on using a RZ1CB-CS disklabel and then editing it
for the Viking parameters, to get around the lack of a Viking 
disktab. It was not necessary.


Try just doing 'disklabel -wr -t ufs /dev/rrz4c viking'

and if that doesn't work, then use a drive (any drive) that does
exist. Example: disklabel -wr -t ufs /dev/rrz4c rz56

then 
# scu -f /dev/rrz4c'
scu> format
...
scu> quit
# disklabel -wr -t ufs /dev/rrz4c viking

Check your result with 'disklabel -rp /dev/rrz4c'
and you should be able to do your newfs commands.

The end result for a Viking looks like, the following. Note that 
the system generated this for me.

