|> The DEC operating system for it is Ultrix, the latest version is 4.5.
|> You _might_ also be able to run NetBSD and OpenBSD on it but I'm not
|> quite sure, the 5500 is a rather rare beast ...

NetBSD doesn't support the 5500.  I think the real stumbling block, is
reworking the NetBSD/vax microvax-3 "mayfair" Q-bus adaptor support so
mips CPUs can use it, and the UBA driver support code so that the
mips-CPU Qbus machines can use it.  Most of the necessary kernel
machinery is already present, it's laregly a cut-and-paste -- the 5100
support took about a day to bash out. The big problem is that nobody
has a suitable machine (5400 or 5500) to test.


Jay Maynard also forwarded me some docs for the SGEC controller and I
have a skeleton driver.


I'm not aware of signficant pmax-specific additions to OpenBSD/pmax,
over and above the NetBSD/pmax codebase they started with.  But I
stopped following their code; an OpenBSD person should really comment.



