In "modern day" DCL I get bitten by this when I forget to put 
an endif, or a endsubprocedure etc...

My solution is to find the offending line, then create a label 
that it can find below it a few lines (scanning the lines between for
syntax errors).  Then moving that label down until DCL can't find it
anymore - then I've at least narrowed it down to where it can and
can't find the label - and I know there is something wrong between
the two.

I usually find the problem this way.


My "test label is usually"

$missing_label:
$ write sys$output "I can find it here"
$ exit

And keep cutting, pasting it futher and futher away (lower) in the 
.com file.

Brian J.
