In article <Pine.GSO.3.96.980808124239.10191A-100000@tardis.tardis.ed.ac.uk>, Tim Austwick <tima@tardis.ed.ac.uk> writes:
|> 
|> I dont have a monitor for this decstation, and i wondered if its possible
|> to connect a dumb terminal (vt22) to it? I read something about typing
|> blind 'setenv console s' but it doesnt seem to do anything.

That works.  You need a null-modem cable and the terminal should be
set for 8 bits, no parity, 9600, connected to the DB-25 on the left,
looking from the rear.  If that doesn't work the PROM is probably
waiting for you to enter the keyboard type/country code.

Try rebooting, waiting about 2 minutes for the selftest to complete,
then type the digit '4' on the LK-201 family keyboard.  Wait another
minute or so and then type the "setenv console s" on the LK-whatever.
You should get a  ">>" prompt on the terminal.

If that doesnt work, power the machine off, open the case, and
physically remove the graphics card.  (Observe anti-static
precautions!)  There is no baseboard graphics on the 3MAXPLUS, and
removing the graphics card will force the PROM to use a serial console.



