In article <35C3F35C.4457@earthlink.net>, "David J. Dachtera" <djesys@earthlink.net> writes:
> Now, if did the FTP as BINARY, you may still be able to salvage the
> download (if not, you're hosed!). Using the /BLOCKSIZE value from
> before, issue a SET FILE/ATTR=LRECL=blksize. That may do it, but I may
> have he qualifier name wrong. Try HELP SET FILE /ATTRIBUTE for the
> correct syntax.

The following is an example of a command that should work, assuming a
valid binary transfer. Substitute the actual blocksize of course -
32256 is the most likely, being the default for an on-disk saveset.

  $ set file whatever/attrib=(lrl:32256,rfm:fix)

Requires VMS V6 or later.  Refer to the OpenVMS FAQ for techniques
for earlier versions.

