A few years back I was working on a cluster which was backed up by a hefty UPS.
When we had a power cut, the machines kept on running.

*But*, when the power came back on the cluster stopped!

Why? The (cheapo 3rd party) terminals weren't on a protected circuit and generated
a break when thy powered up. Like yourself, I was very grateful for the Continue
command!

Over the years I have found simulating a power cut to be a worthwhile exercise.
It's amazing how often the odd router or whatever can find itself on unprotected
circuits as new equipment gets installed and old stuff goes out.

BTW; I don't think much of Hyperterm either. Totally useless in fact!

