Ray Timmons wrote in message <35CA3D48.14A8FE35@aik.tec.sc.us>...
>You know, this is crazy!  When will Intel wake up, kill merced and
>start marketing Alpha?  They do own it now after all.
>
>Is this too obvious or what?


I think you're misinformed.  As has been stated in this group and many press
releases and the general news (those that are accurate, at least)  Intel
Corp does not (read not.  NOT),  Intel Corp does not own Alpha.

Intel's agreement with DEC, before the merger w/ Compaq became official,
sold the manufacturing facilities (buildings & internal equipment).  Also,
many or most or all employees therein became Intel employees.  The agreement
requires Intel to be the manufacturing facility (fab in chip-speak) for DEC
for, IIRC, 'as long as DEC wants Alpha chips manufactured'.  The US
government has imposed a further condition - basically that DEC also have
others able to manufacture the chip for DEC.  Samsung and IBM IIRC.

The ownership of the Alpha intellectual property, name, etc. etc. stayed
with DEC and has merged with DEC to Compaq.





