  our .13 micron technology. This is a technique that minimises
  delays in the interconnect. It uses copper in couple with aluminium
  and it is much cheaper than copper."

  The logic behind Intel's solution is that copper is far less
  plentiful in the world than aluminium, according to a chip analyst.
  Aluminium is extracted from a mineral called bauxite while copper
