As long as we're talking about "real architecture" and the ladders
needed to climb them:

Aluminimum is used for ladders for exactly the same reason aluminum is
used for airplanes: Very good strength/weight ratio.

To do any better, you need to either mix in more magnesium (even
lighter), or go to some space-age material, like carbon/kevlar
reinforced epoxy.

The strongest possible material I have heard about is tubes made out of
bucky-balls, i.e. pure carbon but not in a diamond lattice.

This would tend to make the ladder slightly too expensive to attrack any
buyers, though. :-)

