Richard Jordan <rjordan@MCS.COM> writes:
> Anyone out there conversant with DEC power supplies?  I need too know either 
> likely failure points that I can test for, or where to find an economical
> replacement for this power supply from a VT1200 Xterminal.  The terminal
> works great with the supply from an SZ12.

  What's "economical"? 800-DIGITAL has the H7109-A for $118. If you can use
a H7109-B, that's $90. They claim next-day shipping, 90-day warranty.

> Symptoms; supply is switching, as if it saw a dead short.  LED flickers and
> fan bounces about 2 times per second.  Using an artificial load (resistor 
> load pack from aforementioned SZ12, plus a couple of fans) changed the rate 
> of the pulses slightly, but made no other difference.  No obvious burned
> components, no visible problems noted.

  Who made the supply (is there a vendor logo on it)? Common problems are the
main switch transistor failing, or if the supply was operated at high temps,
the output filter caps may be shot. Look on the tops of the caps for an X-
shaped groove. That's the safety vent. If the top is bowed out at all, replace
the caps.

