Kerry Boguszewski-Odom wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>         I purchased one of the AlphaStations 200 4/233 and a 2.1
> Seagate Barracuda Disk Drive Model No: ST12550WD from www.onsale.com. 
> The drive's SCSI is a 68 pin connection, but the scsi ribbons in my
> alpha do not fit this connection.  Do I need to purchase a different
> ribbon for my alpha or is there an adapter/converter available and
> where would a good place be to obtain one of these converters, if they
> exist?

The drive you have is a wide, differential drive.  You can't use it with
the included SCSI controller (which is only narrow, single-ended).

I'm not sure if you'll be able to use a different controller; if you're
going to be using NT on this system you should be able to; I'm not sure
what 3rd party controllers are supported (if any) under DU 4.0.

