Look for duplicate SCSI ID's.

The NCR 5380 SCSI chip is real robust and does not normally go wonkers
like this. The one thing that can be a real pain and here you'll freak,

The internal Disk Drive Power Wiring. For a while, we had a vendor that
supplied wiring to manufacturing that had the +5VDC and +12VDC reversed.
If a disk was installed on the bus, this usually took out the disks fuse
but also prevented the SCSI from working. Check the wiring and ensure the
SCSI cable is also fine.

