A sad story .....

1. The gift 

Somebody offered me a Micro VAX 3100 -20e for a reasonable price.
After some test I have made the deal.

2. The beginning of a friendship

The Micro VAX was an enrichment under the desk and really "fast",
compared to all other installed under my desk before.

3. The Accident.

Up to the moment, the machine stopped working without being powered
down.
The power supply switch was on, the VAX without power, the green LED
off.
Doesn't matter ... restart.

4. Technical details after the following restart

The console showed the self-test.

KA41-D  V1.0

F_  E  D  C  B  A  9  8  7  6?  5  4  3  2  1

?? 6 80A1 0000 5310

>>>
That's it, no reboot. After manually intervention, the SCSI B-channel
remained disappeared.

5. The tests

>>> T 6
83... Fail

>>> T 50
cut...
?? SCSI-B 0000.5310  V1.58
   FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFF03
FFFFFFFF

>>> T 0
cut...
?? 6 80A1 SCSI-B 6000 0B01

6. Resumee

NO influence of the terminator or the mounted SCSI-B devices is to be
found. The status of SCSI-B remains unchanged. 

On VMS level, no DKB / no MKB device appears, 
>>> show DEVICE on the boot prompt shows no SCSI-B.

7. Try to Repair...

To open the case was not really complicated. Only one IC was installed
two times (the data sheets were pulled from the WWW). It was the SCSI
controller. Oscilloscope heated up and measured quickly, that one did as
requested, the other shows no pleasure to put signals to the SCSI bus.
Decision ... dismount the part and put in a new one ...
AND NOW ....

8. Status

The machine has the same error as before. Nothing has changed, except
for the fact, that the new IC is in a socket and easier to replace ;-) 

9. Questions

