Voltage Regulator Modules
 --------------------------
 Three additional Voltage Regulator Modules (VRM) are now
 available from Digital Equipment Corporation. The part numbers
 are 54-25312-01, 54-25312-02 and 54-25470-01. The J1 jumper
 on the card contains 3 or 4 pairs of pins (depending on the
 part number).

 The jumper pins allow you to set the VRM at various voltage
 settings. This is done by changing the pin location of jumper
 blocks. A jumper block is a small plastic-encased conductor
 (shorting plug) that slips over two pins.

 To change a jumper setting, remove the jumper from its current
 location with your fingers. Place the jumper over the two pins
 designated for the desired setting. Press the jumper evenly onto
 the pins. Be careful not to bend the pins.

 The tables below list the jumper settings for these two VRM parts.
 Pins 1 and 5 (the "5" on some modules is in the wrong place - see
 comments below) are labeled on the card. "On" means that a jumper

 block has been slipped over the two pins. "Off" means that the
 jumper block is not enclosing the two pins.


 54-25312-01: J1 Jumper Settings

 ......setting
 1-2...3-4...5-6...voltage...Processor
 ---------------------------------
 Off...Off...Off...2.8v......Intel Pentium w/MMX 166/200 MHz
 On....Off...Off...2.9v......AMD-K6 166/200 MHz
 Off...On....Off...3.0v
 On....On....Off...3.1v
 Off...Off...On....3.2v......AMD-K6 233 MHz
 On....Off...On....3.3v
 Off...On....On....3.4v
 On....On....On....3.5v......Intel Pentium or AMD-K5 166/200 MHz


 54-25312-02 and 54-25470-01: J1 Jumper Settings

 .............setting
 1-2...3-4...5-6...7-8...voltage...Processor
 -------------------------------------------
 On....Off...Off...Off...2.1v
 Off...On....Off...Off...2.2v......AMD-K6 266 MHz
 On....On....Off...Off...2.3v
 Off...Off...On....Off...2.4v
 On....Off...On....Off...2.5v
 Off...On....On....Off...2.6v
 On....On....On....Off...2.7v
 Off...Off...Off...On....2.8v......Intel Pentium w/MMX 166/200 MHz
 On....Off...Off...On....2.9v......AMD-K6 166/200 MHz
 Off...On....Off...On....3.0v
 On....On....Off...On....3.1v
 Off...Off...On....On....3.2v......AMD-K6 233 MHz
 On....Off...On....On....3.3v
 Off...On....On....On....3.4v
 On....On....On....On....3.5v...Intel Pent. or AMD-K5 166/200 MHz

 Comments:
 When looking at the VRM jumpers, pin pair 1-2 is closest to the
 middle of the module.

 On some of the VRM's there is a "5" printed above the pins, ignore
 the number it is in the wrong place.

