> I have the same problem with you. I also bid from onsale.

Multia/UDB computer have a scsi chip on the motherboard and most
have a scsi connector on the back. SCSI was *not an option*.  

At the (srm prompt) >>> , type 'show device' and you should see:
 ...
 ...
 ewa0.0.0.11.0	EWA0	08-00-2b-3a-ff-22
 pka0.7.0.6.0	PKA0	SCSI Bus ID 7

If that entry is missing and your Multia is not small enough
to fit in a briefcase, then you probably don't have a Multia. (-:

If the PKA0 does show up then you probably just need a scsi cable
to go to the chassis. It is possible that you have one of the
semi-useless early models that were missing the external scsi,
the PCI slot and sometimes even the floppy drive. (some VX40s)

You should go to: http://www.brouhaha.com/~eric/computers/udb.html

Make a point of downloading the udb-man.pdf file. This is the
116 page Multia manual.

Charlie

