chrisl@interlog.com wrote in message <6q09ml$27d$1@news.interlog.com>...
>I have a saveset that I picked up via ftp from a client site.
>When I try to restore it I encounter bad crc, block size errors.
>Someone told me that I can use the convert utility to fix this but I don't
>know how.
>Can anyone help?
>thanks

The problem are the file attributes. You can use the set file command to
restore the correct attributes.
Savesets are fixed lenght sequential files. Install kits and tape savesets
usually have a block size of 8192. Disk savesets are created with  a block
size of 32256.
Try the fillowing command:

set file tt_exe.sav /attrib=(rfm:fix,rat:none,lrl:32256)

If you still get errors fiddle a with the block size (lrl parameter).
--
Jens.Schluetter at TradingTechnologies dot com







